{title: Chief Omar}
{subtitle: Genesis 36:11; 36:15; 1 Chronicles 1:36; Genesis 36:9–16}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In the hill country of [C]Seir the line began
[Bb]Esau the father of the E[Dm]domites is named
Eliphaz his firstborn son [C]from Adah came
And the [Bb]chiefs a[C]mong his de[Dm]scendants rose to fame
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Chief Teman and Chief Omar stand [Bb]tall
[C]Chief Zepho and Chief Kenaz [Dm]answer the call
Descended from Eliphaz in the [Bb]land of Edom
Their [C]history is written in the [Dm]family song
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The sons of Eliphaz [C]are listed by name
Te[Bb]man Omar Zepho Gatam [Dm]and Kenaz are the same
They formed the foundation of [C]the tribes so dear
[Bb]Settled in the mountains for [Dm]generations near
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] | [Dm] | ×2

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
From Adam to the end the ge[C]nealogy flows
One [Bb]Chronicles confirms [Dm]what the record knows
Omar is a chief in the [C]line of Esau
[Bb]His place in the history is [Dm]firmly drawn
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Chief Omar is named in the [Bb]book of Genesis
A [C]tribal leader in the [Dm]land of Edom
{end_of_verse}
